[36m(TaskRunner pid=122980)[0m - \( 97_b = 9 \cdot b + 7 \)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122980)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122980)[0m We need \( b + 7 \) to divide \( 9b + 7 \). This can be expressed as:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122980)[0m \[ 9b + 7 = k \cdot (b + 7) \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122980)[0m for some integer \( k \).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122980)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122980)[0m Rearranging this equation, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122980)[0m \[ 9b + 7 = k \cdot b + 7k \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122980)[0m \[ 9b - kb = 7k - 7 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122980)[0m \[ b(9 - k) = 7(k - 1) \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122980)[0m \[ b = \frac{7(k - 1)}{9 - k} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122980)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122980)[0m For \( b \) to be an integer greater than 9, \( \frac{7(k - 1)}{9 - k} \) must be an integer. We denote \( d = 9 - k \), so the equation becomes:
